+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN BEHAVIOR -->
+### Behavior
+
+In laneless driving, when the model path sits inside the lane center in a corner, the set share of that difference is added to the target curvature toward the lane center. The correction only points outward. It blends in gradually over about 2 s and also fades out gradually when it stops, so it turns on and off without a step (about 0.15 s when the driver steers).
+
+- **Higher:** Changes the target curvature to remove more of the inside bias.
+- **0:** Nothing is computed; behavior is unchanged.
+- **Conditions:** Acts only when both lane-line probabilities and standard deviations are good, the lane is 2.5–4.5 m wide and steady, the model follows the lane, corner lateral acceleration and curvature are large enough, and speed is above about 30 km/h.
+- **Pauses:** No correction during a lane change, automatic turn or turn signal and for 1 s afterward, during driver steering and for 0.5 s afterward, or when a moving radar vehicle or BSD is present in the adjacent lane on the corner outside.
+- **Scope:** Applies only to the laneless target curvature. It does not apply to the lane-mode path or to Volkswagen MEB.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END BEHAVIOR -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN USAGE -->
+### Usage
+
+Defaults to off. To try it, start low and check both whether the car still hugs the inside of corners and whether steering shakes. Return to `0` if anything is wrong.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END USAGE -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN REFERENCE -->
+### Reference
+
+<!-- CARROT:NOTICE level="WARNING" -->
+> [!WARNING]
+> Experimental and not validated on a vehicle. It was checked only by replaying recorded drive logs as fixed input. 50% does not move the vehicle by 50%; the actual shift is smaller because the model pulls back.
+<!-- CARROT:NOTICE:END -->
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END REFERENCE -->
 <!-- CARROT:MANUAL:END LatCornerCenterBlend -->
 
